      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Account and Project\nA global connection,\n`dbtcloud_global_connection`, belongs to the\naccount and holds the details of one data\nplatform, such as a Snowflake account. A\nproject does not point to a connection. Each\nenvironment of the project does, with\n`connection_id` ([environment doc](https://git\nhub.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/b\nlob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment.md#L72)\n). So one connection can serve many projects.\n\nA project holds the rest:\n\n- `dbtcloud_repository` names the Git\nrepository. `dbtcloud_project_repository`\nlinks it to the project.\n- A credential, such as\n`dbtcloud_snowflake_credential`, holds the\nuser, role, schema and secret that one\ndeployment environment uses.\n- `dbtcloud_environment` combines a\nconnection, a credential and code settings.\n- `dbtcloud_environment_variable` holds one\nvariable with a value for each environment.\n- `dbtcloud_job` holds the commands that run\nin one environment.\n\nProvider version 1.0.0 removed the older\nconnection resources, such as\n`dbtcloud_connection` and\n`dbtcloud_project_connection`.\n`dbtcloud_global_connection` replaces them\n([upgrade guide](https://github.com/dbt-labs/t\nerraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/g\nuides/90_upgrading_from_v0_to_v1.md#L7-L12)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-76d1ab9bd7d5",
      "originalText": "Account and Project\nA global connection, `dbtcloud_global_connection`, belongs to the account and holds the details of one data platform, such as a Snowflake account. A project does not point to a connection. Each environment of the project does, with `connection_id` ([environment doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment.md#L72)). So one connection can serve many projects.\n\nA project holds the rest:\n\n- `dbtcloud_repository` names the Git repository. `dbtcloud_project_repository` links it to the project.\n- A credential, such as `dbtcloud_snowflake_credential`, holds the user, role, schema and secret that one deployment environment uses.\n- `dbtcloud_environment` combines a connection, a credential and code settings.\n- `dbtcloud_environment_variable` holds one variable with a value for each environment.\n- `dbtcloud_job` holds the commands that run in one environment.\n\nProvider version 1.0.0 removed the older connection resources, such as `dbtcloud_connection` and `dbtcloud_project_connection`. `dbtcloud_global_connection` replaces them ([upgrade guide](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/guides/90_upgrading_from_v0_to_v1.md#L7-L12)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "account-and-project"
      }
    },
