      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Environment Decides Where\nAn environment is either `development` or\n`deployment`. A project has one development\nenvironment and as many deployment\nenvironments as needed ([environment doc](http\ns://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbt\ncloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment.\nmd#L11)). Each environment sets four things ([\narguments](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terrafo\nrm-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resourc\nes/environment.md#L72-L83)):\n\n- `connection_id`: the data platform.\n- `credential_id`: the identity for deployment\nruns. A development environment has none,\nbecause each developer sets their own\ncredentials in dbt Cloud.\n- `dbt_version`: for example `latest` or\n`versionless`.\n- `custom_branch`: the Git branch to run.\n\nA job adds what to run and when:\n`execute_steps` holds the dbt commands,\n`triggers` holds the trigger flags, and\n`target_name` sets the value of `target.name`\nin the models ([job doc](https://github.com/db\nt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.\n1/docs/resources/job.md#L216-L246)). A model\nthat checks `target.name` therefore behaves\naccording to the job, not the environment.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-c18e8b9521f0",
      "originalText": "The Environment Decides Where\nAn environment is either `development` or `deployment`. A project has one development environment and as many deployment environments as needed ([environment doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment.md#L11)). Each environment sets four things ([arguments](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment.md#L72-L83)):\n\n- `connection_id`: the data platform.\n- `credential_id`: the identity for deployment runs. A development environment has none, because each developer sets their own credentials in dbt Cloud.\n- `dbt_version`: for example `latest` or `versionless`.\n- `custom_branch`: the Git branch to run.\n\nA job adds what to run and when: `execute_steps` holds the dbt commands, `triggers` holds the trigger flags, and `target_name` sets the value of `target.name` in the models ([job doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/job.md#L216-L246)). A model that checks `target.name` therefore behaves according to the job, not the environment.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "the-environment-decides-where"
      }
    },
    {
