      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What the Provider Reads Back\nA refresh reads most settings of jobs and\nenvironments from dbt Cloud. So an edit in the\ndbt Cloud UI to such a setting shows in the\nnext plan, and the apply reverts it. The\n[Terraform map](../terraform.md#outside-change\ns-get-reverted-outside-changes-get-reverted)\nshows the same effect with Snowflake.\n\nSecrets are the exception. The dbt Cloud API\nmasks them, so the provider cannot read them\nback. For an environment variable whose name\nstarts with `DBT_ENV_SECRET`, the provider\nkeeps the values from its own state\n([environment variable code](https://github.co\nm/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1\n.13.1/pkg/framework/objects/environment_variab\nle/resource.go#L161-L182)). A secret that\nsomeone changes in the UI therefore never\nshows in a plan, and the next apply does not\nrestore it either.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-521a2d4b4f29",
      "originalText": "What the Provider Reads Back\nA refresh reads most settings of jobs and environments from dbt Cloud. So an edit in the dbt Cloud UI to such a setting shows in the next plan, and the apply reverts it. The [Terraform map](../terraform.md#outside-changes-get-reverted-outside-changes-get-reverted) shows the same effect with Snowflake.\n\nSecrets are the exception. The dbt Cloud API masks them, so the provider cannot read them back. For an environment variable whose name starts with `DBT_ENV_SECRET`, the provider keeps the values from its own state ([environment variable code](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/pkg/framework/objects/environment_variable/resource.go#L161-L182)). A secret that someone changes in the UI therefore never shows in a plan, and the next apply does not restore it either.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "what-the-provider-reads-back"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
