    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2903084597,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-ea15b27ee859",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1900.0,
      "y": 2439.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 350.0,
      "seed": 854347,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Secrets in State and Out of Sight\nThe private key and passphrase of a credential\nare stored in the state in plain text;\n`sensitive` only hides them in plan output\n([credential doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/\nterraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/\nresources/snowflake_credential.md#L62)). The\nvalues of environment variables are not even\nmarked sensitive ([variable doc](https://githu\nb.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blo\nb/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment_variable.\nmd#L39)). Newer 1.x versions add write-only\narguments such as `private_key_wo`, which keep\na secret out of the state; they need Terraform\n1.11 or later ([credential doc](https://github\n.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob\n/v1.13.1/docs/resources/snowflake_credential.m\nd#L26-L27)). And a secret changed in the UI\nstays invisible to Terraform, as What the\nProvider Reads Back explains.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-ea15b27ee859",
      "originalText": "Secrets in State and Out of Sight\nThe private key and passphrase of a credential are stored in the state in plain text; `sensitive` only hides them in plan output ([credential doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/snowflake_credential.md#L62)). The values of environment variables are not even marked sensitive ([variable doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/environment_variable.md#L39)). Newer 1.x versions add write-only arguments such as `private_key_wo`, which keep a secret out of the state; they need Terraform 1.11 or later ([credential doc](https://github.com/dbt-labs/terraform-provider-dbtcloud/blob/v1.13.1/docs/resources/snowflake_credential.md#L26-L27)). And a secret changed in the UI stays invisible to Terraform, as What the Provider Reads Back explains.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "secrets-in-state"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9665000385,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-cd65dbccb6e3",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
